It's just over a month left to x-mas and I came up with these ideas last
night:

* If you start (or load) a game on December 25:th (and 24:th, that's when
Santa comes in Sweden) there is a chance that Santa Claus (a fat red @) is
generated (only once per game) and gives you a present.
* The present should be a new type of container that only can be looted once
to take out what's inside.
* I'm not sure what the gift should be. Not a weapon or anything else you
use to hurt others with (Santa's a nice guy), maybe a (non-attack) spell
book, a piece of armor (boots, gloves, shirts, cloaks and "soft" suits) or a
tool.
* He should try to give you something you don't already have.
* If you reed the present it should say something like "To <name> from
Santa" and then some hint of what's inside (good place for YAFM).
* Maybe he should only give a present if you have been good. But I don't
know how to measure that. Alignment does not work because I don't think
Santa and your god has the same definition of what's good.
* Maybe Santa should have his reindeers with him (what monster type? 'u' or
'q' or ...)
* Killing Santa (or any of his reindeers) should come with a (luck?)
penalty.
* Maybe he should give presents to monsters too.

What do you think?

It's supposed to mostly be a fun thing sort of an easer egg (I'll be back
with another YANI when that season comes closer =)

I'm not sure if I can implement this, but I might try if I get the time (not
too likely though). If someone else feels like doing it just go ahead, but
tell me so I can try it out.

